WEBVTT

00:01.910 --> 00:06.290
After New Year, entrance exams
for private schools will finally begin.

00:06.430 --> 00:09.140
Make sure you keep studying until then.

00:09.300 --> 00:11.640
Winter break starts next week.

00:13.570 --> 00:15.610
I'm going to graduate soon!

00:15.750 --> 00:18.610
T-there's no time left!

00:20.230 --> 00:22.890
So what's this important stuff
you're going to talk about?

00:22.990 --> 00:24.400
Listen carefully.

00:24.400 --> 00:28.060
Kijibayashi and I will graduate
in three months.

00:28.190 --> 00:30.570
There will only be
Inukawa and Saruta left.

00:30.570 --> 00:33.840
That would naturally mean Brainwave Club
is going to be terminated.

00:34.460 --> 00:36.640
Isn't that just sad?

00:36.840 --> 00:39.510
-What's so sad about it?
-Huh?

00:39.840 --> 00:42.550
We're not going to make
any memories at this rate.

00:42.550 --> 00:45.120
Think back to everything we did so far!

00:47.060 --> 00:49.010
But we have some memories,

00:49.010 --> 00:51.320
like eating snacks and chatting
while lazing around.

00:51.450 --> 00:53.850
There's also playing cards and games.

00:53.950 --> 00:56.360
No, I'm not talking about
that kind of stuff.

00:56.360 --> 00:57.224
-Huh?
-Huh?

00:57.650 --> 00:59.250
Huh?

01:08.860 --> 01:10.080
Wait, what?

01:10.080 --> 01:11.550
Why are you crying?

01:11.610 --> 01:13.310
Is your stomach hurting?

01:13.310 --> 01:15.480
Did your exam go that badly?

01:15.480 --> 01:17.140
I mean, I'm no better, but...

01:17.370 --> 01:20.510
We didn't make any progress
on our research for telepathy!

01:20.510 --> 01:22.290
This is our only chance!

01:22.360 --> 01:24.110
Is it something worth crying over?

01:24.160 --> 01:26.920
Y-you can try better
at high school, right?

01:26.980 --> 01:31.740
So, you were actually serious about
wanting to communicate with aliens?

01:31.840 --> 01:34.070
Of course I am...

01:34.220 --> 01:36.790
I'm also going to continue it as a hobby.

01:36.930 --> 01:41.330
But this is the only time where I get
to spend time with you guys.

01:41.950 --> 01:47.130
You guys are the only ones who would
join a club with this weird goal.

01:47.400 --> 01:51.530
This place is a special place for me!

01:52.480 --> 01:54.960
Hey, what do you guys think?

01:55.330 --> 01:56.760
Well, uhh...

01:56.760 --> 01:58.240
What do you think, Inukawa?

01:58.240 --> 02:02.960
Well, uhh, let's hear from
the youngest first.

02:03.070 --> 02:05.990
Umm, telepathy is...

02:06.090 --> 02:08.940
Sorry, what was our goal again?

02:16.870 --> 02:19.880
Wow, incredible lung capacity...

02:25.240 --> 02:28.110
Thank you for everything, you three.

02:28.920 --> 02:31.960
The Brainwave Club is hereby disbanded.

02:31.960 --> 02:34.130
It was pretty fun.

02:37.660 --> 02:40.230
Wait, we're really disbanded?

02:41.710 --> 02:47.580
Seems like Kurata is way more serious
about this than we ever thought.

02:49.510 --> 02:54.360
I guess we should give
all the books in here a read?

03:00.450 --> 03:02.160
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:03.280 --> 03:05.030
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:06.200 --> 03:07.870
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:09.040 --> 03:10.710
(MOB MOB WOW!)

03:12.120 --> 03:14.840
I realized that our youth is gray

03:14.840 --> 03:17.760
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

03:17.840 --> 03:20.260
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

03:20.260 --> 03:23.430
Struggling through this adolescence

03:23.550 --> 03:26.390
Don't disturb my deep psyche

03:26.390 --> 03:29.060
Who is that behind you?

03:29.180 --> 03:32.850
Opposing ideas create distortion

03:32.850 --> 03:36.270
Exorcise all the sorrow

03:36.440 --> 03:39.940
So, do what you can now

03:40.030 --> 03:41.860
My life

03:42.110 --> 03:45.990
Finally, break it down

03:47.490 --> 03:50.330
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

03:50.330 --> 03:53.210
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

03:53.210 --> 03:55.960
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

03:55.960 --> 03:58.920
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

03:58.920 --> 04:01.420
Taking things as it is

04:01.420 --> 04:04.840
In this free relation where
We resent each other

04:04.930 --> 04:07.140
Once these two become one

04:07.140 --> 04:09.140
That smile becomes one

04:09.140 --> 04:12.230
And only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

04:12.890 --> 04:15.900
"1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

04:16.230 --> 04:17.310
(MOB MOB WOW!)

04:17.310 --> 04:20.190
One and only "1"
(MOB MOB WOW!)

04:20.360 --> 04:21.900
"1"

04:21.900 --> 04:23.070
(MOB MOB WOW!)

04:23.070 --> 04:25.360
One and only "1"

04:26.950 --> 04:31.450
(Communicating 1 ~Winter Break~)

04:35.260 --> 04:36.740
Brother.

04:37.900 --> 04:41.260
There's some guests for you.
They're waiting outside.

04:42.040 --> 04:43.670
Who is it?

04:44.430 --> 04:46.800
It seems pretty cold outside.

04:47.850 --> 04:49.540
Are you okay?

04:49.640 --> 04:50.900
What do you mean?

04:50.900 --> 04:54.250
It's been a month since
Dimple last showed up.

04:54.250 --> 04:55.920
Is it still bothering you?

04:56.010 --> 04:58.900
Oh, I was just spacing off.

04:59.740 --> 05:01.230
I see.

05:04.140 --> 05:05.140
Huh?

05:05.140 --> 05:07.210
Everyone? What's going on?

05:07.300 --> 05:12.170
Mob! Why didn't you pick up your phone?
We called you several times!

05:12.270 --> 05:14.450
Sorry, I didn't notice.

05:14.600 --> 05:16.470
Did you need something?

05:16.660 --> 05:20.280
Please, can't you use
your powers for telepathy?

05:21.360 --> 05:24.250
We acted as if we knew
while we actually didn't!

05:24.250 --> 05:26.830
We underestimated what
being a youth means!

05:26.830 --> 05:29.070
Inukawa, calm down.

05:29.200 --> 05:30.970
What is going on?

05:32.800 --> 05:36.140
I see, so Tome quit.

05:36.450 --> 05:39.630
I think she's just prioritizing
her entrance exams.

05:40.440 --> 05:43.400
But I can't use telepathy.

05:43.480 --> 05:45.260
Can't you make it work somehow?

05:45.330 --> 05:48.860
Umm, I know someone
that can use telepathy.

05:49.100 --> 05:50.630
Huh?

05:52.200 --> 05:55.660
If the target is the space,
then I'm afraid we can't help.

05:55.850 --> 05:59.380
Our telepathy only works
between us siblings.

05:59.550 --> 06:00.920
I see.

06:00.920 --> 06:04.140
Yeah, of course
it wouldn't be that easy...

06:04.450 --> 06:05.760
But...

06:05.760 --> 06:11.610
We might be able to find other telepaths
if someone stronger helped.

06:11.710 --> 06:16.700
Yeah, but only if there is someone
who can receive our telepathy.

06:16.780 --> 06:17.940
Huh?

06:18.520 --> 06:22.010
It might be impossible to send
a specific message to someone,

06:22.120 --> 06:25.210
but we can spread
a noise around us.

06:25.420 --> 06:26.620
Noise?

06:26.620 --> 06:30.550
It's an unpleasant sound
that only telepaths can hear.

06:30.640 --> 06:33.390
So, something like an ear ringing?

06:33.390 --> 06:35.030
So you're going to call them?

06:35.100 --> 06:38.900
Yes, but it depends on the person
receiving it themselves.

06:38.970 --> 06:44.660
If we keep emitting the noise, they might
try to approach the source of the noise.

06:44.840 --> 06:47.260
But we won't know
what kind of person it is, then?

06:47.320 --> 06:48.770
That's kinda scary, isn't it?

06:48.770 --> 06:52.220
But they're our only hope.

06:52.990 --> 06:55.100
What do we do, Brother?

06:55.240 --> 06:58.390
This is for Tome, right?
Let's do it.

06:58.470 --> 07:00.480
What can I do to help?

07:00.570 --> 07:03.640
He seems really dependable
for some reason...

07:03.720 --> 07:08.760
It's cold here, so how about we first move
to the club room for a strategy meeting?

07:10.450 --> 07:12.410
-Go go go!
-Pass here!

07:12.660 --> 07:16.250
Right now, thank's to Teru's training,

07:16.250 --> 07:20.080
we can communicate up to
three kilometers if we do our best.

07:20.250 --> 07:23.550
I managed to receive the message
to buy natto

07:23.550 --> 07:25.150
on the way home the other day.

07:25.270 --> 07:28.300
You could've just used a phone
rather than trying hard.

07:28.450 --> 07:30.990
But if we fire the noise
in all directions,

07:30.990 --> 07:33.920
then we'll probably only
manage around 500 meters.

07:34.010 --> 07:36.010
That's not very far...

07:36.090 --> 07:40.330
If Kageyama helps
and amplifies our output,

07:40.330 --> 07:43.680
I think we can double
or triple our noise range.

07:43.800 --> 07:46.350
Whoa, that's amazing.

07:46.560 --> 07:49.650
Wait, is Mob's brother also a psychic?!

07:49.800 --> 07:52.300
My brother would be better at this.

07:52.650 --> 07:56.910
Let's give it a try.
I'll try to make it as wide as possible.

07:57.110 --> 08:00.650
Thanks for calling us
for this interesting experiment.

08:00.840 --> 08:03.830
We can finally pay you back,
Kageyama.

08:04.010 --> 08:06.290
All right, let's try this, Kaito.

08:06.290 --> 08:09.430
Yeah. Let's do our best, Brother.

08:12.380 --> 08:15.380
We're currently emitting the noise.

08:15.810 --> 08:18.240
We can't hear anything...

08:18.430 --> 08:20.680
But yeah, do your thing, Mob.

08:25.580 --> 08:28.100
I'm sending some power your way.

08:28.100 --> 08:29.760
Please do.

08:37.600 --> 08:39.720
T-this is amazing!

08:40.160 --> 08:42.830
Even I can faintly hear it.

08:44.510 --> 08:46.960
I-it feels like my head
is about to split open!

08:47.040 --> 08:50.550
I can add some more,
but I guess we shouldn't do that.

08:50.820 --> 08:53.750
It's okay, we'll push it to the limit.

08:54.050 --> 08:55.720
You don't have to push
yourselves that far!

08:55.790 --> 08:58.040
This is the only way!

08:58.040 --> 09:00.040
Please do it!

09:02.930 --> 09:05.430
Whoa, I'm getting goosebumps.

09:05.430 --> 09:06.950
Y-yeah, me too.

09:06.950 --> 09:09.420
Is it affecting the human body?

09:09.500 --> 09:10.990
Who is it?

09:11.370 --> 09:13.700
Whoa, that scared me.

09:13.700 --> 09:16.150
What are you guys doing here?

09:16.230 --> 09:18.580
Oh, it's just Takenaka.

09:18.750 --> 09:20.010
Who is he?

09:20.010 --> 09:22.300
A former member of the Brainwave Club.

09:22.400 --> 09:26.120
The Brainwave Club was abolished
because he quit on us.

09:27.160 --> 09:30.470
Why are you back here now, anyway?
You're in the Tennis Club, right?

09:30.590 --> 09:34.560
Oh, we still have club activities
even on winter break.

09:34.640 --> 09:38.840
They're making us run around
the perimeters in this stupid cold weather.

09:39.500 --> 09:42.680
I mean, that's what you signed up for.

09:42.750 --> 09:45.610
So I waited for a chance to slip away.

09:45.710 --> 09:48.920
I was thinking of taking it easy
in this room.

09:49.200 --> 09:52.590
I knew it, you're actually just like us.

09:53.520 --> 09:55.420
By the way, what are you doing?

09:55.530 --> 09:57.490
We're looking for telepaths.

09:57.490 --> 09:59.490
These people are psychics.

09:59.560 --> 10:00.550
What?

10:00.550 --> 10:02.530
Are you for real?

10:03.120 --> 10:05.790
You guys are still doing
that kind of thing?

10:05.790 --> 10:07.030
That's so stupid!

10:07.030 --> 10:11.650
This is why people think the Brainwave Club
is full of weirdos and creeps.

10:11.730 --> 10:13.880
Get a grip already.

10:13.930 --> 10:15.360
Oh, shut up.

10:15.360 --> 10:18.440
We're just finally getting
serious now, okay?

10:18.440 --> 10:20.600
If you're going to get in our way,
please leave.

10:20.710 --> 10:24.810
Fine, I'll leave once I warm myself a bit.

10:26.520 --> 10:28.970
All right, let's do it one more time.

10:28.970 --> 10:31.230
It was going pretty well.

10:31.230 --> 10:34.010
Yeah, if we do it multiple times
during this winter break,

10:34.010 --> 10:37.620
a real telepath might actually show up.

10:38.020 --> 10:39.450
All right, ready...

10:39.600 --> 10:41.010
...go!

10:42.520 --> 10:46.030
Hey, you self-proclaimed psychics.

10:46.030 --> 10:49.680
What the heck are you guys doing
with such a serious face?

10:54.300 --> 10:56.910
Aren't you guys embarrassed?

10:59.990 --> 11:01.910
It's getting even stronger?

11:02.000 --> 11:03.760
Just a little more push.

11:05.740 --> 11:08.460
Even my head starts to hurt.

11:11.660 --> 11:13.920
Can't you guys just stop...?

11:14.010 --> 11:17.050
What's wrong, Takenaka?
You're looking kinda pale.

11:17.210 --> 11:19.520
Do you have a fever or something?

11:30.920 --> 11:33.560
You're so noisy, goddammit!

11:36.320 --> 11:38.550
Just...

11:39.780 --> 11:42.250
Just stop that noise already.

11:50.220 --> 11:54.350
I find out I'm different from others
when I was five.

11:55.100 --> 12:02.240
The kindergarten teacher's thoughts and
speech are different, but nobody noticed.

12:02.940 --> 12:05.500
Then when I voiced
my father's real thoughts,

12:05.500 --> 12:07.420
my mother broke down crying.

12:07.520 --> 12:10.390
That's when I realized it's not something
I'm supposed to do.

12:13.300 --> 12:16.530
Others' thoughts just simply
came to my head.

12:16.730 --> 12:19.850
As I grew up,
they grow even louder,

12:20.000 --> 12:22.650
and the range from where
I can receive them also grows.

12:22.650 --> 12:24.800
It was such a pain.

12:25.130 --> 12:30.520
I think it was around third grade
when I can send my thoughts to others.

12:31.320 --> 12:35.810
You always carry snacks
with you, that's nice.

12:35.810 --> 12:39.790
I have tons of them back at home.
I'll bring some next time.

12:40.000 --> 12:43.460
-Really? Then I want some crackling gum.
-I'll go shoplifting again.

12:45.260 --> 12:47.750
Are you stupid?
You're going to get arrested!

12:49.470 --> 12:50.760
What's wrong?

12:50.860 --> 12:52.670
Return it to the shop!

12:52.670 --> 12:55.020
O-okay!

12:56.880 --> 12:59.840
After that, to let off some steam,

12:59.840 --> 13:04.780
I assaulted someone by yelling
inside their head every day.

13:05.580 --> 13:09.220
Y-you always lived like that?

13:09.610 --> 13:11.680
I don't do that anymore, Inukawa.

13:11.680 --> 13:13.920
-Wha?!
-What's wrong?

13:14.040 --> 13:16.810
He spoke... directly in my head?

13:16.860 --> 13:19.030
Kijibayashi, Saruta.

13:21.030 --> 13:22.590
Really?

13:23.290 --> 13:27.360
He's kinda scary.
Telepaths are abnormal.

13:27.470 --> 13:29.580
Yeah, I guess so.

13:29.660 --> 13:32.350
I am an abnormal existence.

13:32.350 --> 13:33.810
But don't worry.

13:33.810 --> 13:38.000
I've learned how to keep other's thoughts
from entering my head.

13:38.120 --> 13:41.960
I've had enough of listening to what
others think. It makes me sick.

13:42.220 --> 13:44.700
That's why I always wear an earplug.

13:44.700 --> 13:47.320
I sealed this ability away.

13:47.630 --> 13:51.690
But then I hear this
really stupid loud noise.

13:51.880 --> 13:55.130
Oh, right, sorry about that.

13:55.250 --> 13:57.530
We're looking for telepaths.

13:57.530 --> 13:58.880
Will you help us?

13:58.880 --> 14:00.860
Why now?

14:01.120 --> 14:03.520
You're not actually interested
in telepathy, right?

14:03.620 --> 14:05.400
No, we're serious here!

14:05.400 --> 14:07.970
You'll know it's true
if you read our thoughts!

14:08.470 --> 14:12.620
I don't want to make any more
bad memories with telepathy.

14:12.710 --> 14:15.210
I'm not going to take off
my earplug either.

14:15.210 --> 14:16.910
Go ask someone else.

14:17.400 --> 14:19.790
You were looking for friends,
didn't you?

14:20.210 --> 14:21.400
What?

14:21.480 --> 14:23.940
You joined this club

14:23.940 --> 14:28.700
because you thought there might
be someone like you, right?

14:29.580 --> 14:31.370
Yeah, that's right.

14:31.460 --> 14:33.370
But that was a mistake.

14:33.370 --> 14:35.520
It's just some occult research club.

14:36.300 --> 14:42.520
That's why I stopped having the faint hope
that there is someone else like me.

14:44.240 --> 14:48.620
I have no plan of being used to make
some "fun memories" for you people.

14:48.710 --> 14:50.350
Being used...

14:50.350 --> 14:54.700
If you think that's all there is to it,
then it's okay if you don't want to help.

14:55.070 --> 14:57.920
That is, if you really aren't interested.

14:58.000 --> 15:00.080
What are you trying to say?

15:00.810 --> 15:04.840
I also have times when
I'm fed up with my powers.

15:04.990 --> 15:08.170
Even if I try to hide it,
it's still an inseparable part of me.

15:08.910 --> 15:10.760
If there are others that need your powers,

15:10.760 --> 15:15.010
then I think accepting their request
can sometimes be enjoyable.

15:16.320 --> 15:19.630
What's with the high and mighty act?
Don't act like you know me.

15:20.220 --> 15:22.350
It's my true feeling.

15:30.010 --> 15:33.410
W-well, I don't want you
to make that noise again.

15:33.410 --> 15:36.410
I guess I'll help, just this once.

15:37.830 --> 15:40.190
Thanks! We'll be in your debt,
Takenaka!

15:40.190 --> 15:41.370
-Yay!
-Yay!

15:41.370 --> 15:43.790
-We did it!
-Thanks a lot, you two!

15:44.080 --> 15:45.710
Takenaka.

15:46.360 --> 15:49.820
Did you... read my brother's mind?

15:49.820 --> 15:51.350
You're his little brother, huh?

15:51.450 --> 15:53.360
Now then, did I?

15:53.470 --> 15:56.800
You have a complex about not being able
to relate with your brother?

15:56.890 --> 15:59.370
Is that what my thoughts are saying?!

15:59.440 --> 16:01.760
Nah, I'm just guessing.

16:01.900 --> 16:05.920
I have my earplugs, but I can still
guess somewhat from your eyes.

16:06.060 --> 16:09.350
I think those kinds of things
should be cherished.

16:10.900 --> 16:13.740
So, what am I supposed to do?

16:16.370 --> 16:17.520
Here.

16:17.520 --> 16:21.200
It's a purifying kelp tea that we've
just begun accepting mail-order recently.

16:21.340 --> 16:24.600
Winter also affects those
kinds of spiritual things,

16:24.600 --> 16:26.830
so please make sure
to keep yourself hydrated.

16:26.830 --> 16:30.290
Dehydration leads
to poor blood circulation,

16:30.290 --> 16:35.630
so it might invite evil spirits that cause
fatigue and poor sleeping habits.

16:35.720 --> 16:37.390
Ooh...

16:37.980 --> 16:39.730
Thank you very much.

16:39.730 --> 16:42.790
I will visit you again, Master Reigen.

16:46.640 --> 16:48.810
Even my body feels sluggish.

16:48.950 --> 16:52.030
It's hard to get any motivation
when it's this cold, yeah?

16:52.640 --> 16:53.920
What are you doing?

16:53.980 --> 16:58.010
It's homework from school.
I have to finish it during winter break.

16:58.010 --> 16:59.470
Winter break, huh?

16:59.470 --> 17:02.580
Being a student sure is nice,
having events like that and all.

17:03.080 --> 17:05.450
How about we go drinking for once?

17:05.600 --> 17:10.740
Sorry, I have a year-end party
with friends from night school today.

17:10.840 --> 17:12.280
I see...

17:14.450 --> 17:17.070
Oh, Mob? What's wrong?

17:17.370 --> 17:20.980
Plans for New Year's Eve?
I don't have any for now.

17:21.080 --> 17:23.220
Are you going on a shrine visit
on New Year?

17:23.420 --> 17:24.620
What?

17:24.620 --> 17:26.270
Mud Boat Mountain?

17:26.380 --> 17:28.040
UFO?

17:28.760 --> 17:32.320
Fine, fine. I'll do it.

17:35.330 --> 17:38.380
I gotta go for some UFO searching
at the end of the year.

17:38.380 --> 17:42.570
They called me just so they
could get me to rent a car.

17:42.730 --> 17:48.110
Man, why do I have to babysit
on New Year's Eve?

17:48.270 --> 17:50.870
I'm happy for you, Reigen.

17:51.800 --> 17:54.140
What? Mud Boat Mountain?

17:54.140 --> 17:55.990
I'm not going.

17:56.080 --> 17:58.300
Got a winter training camp
with my cram school.

17:58.300 --> 18:00.330
The Brainwave Club is already
disbanded anyway,

18:00.330 --> 18:02.860
just do whatever you want.

18:05.190 --> 18:06.710
She said she isn't coming...

18:06.710 --> 18:09.530
Seriously, President Kurata?

18:09.610 --> 18:13.100
I guess we just have to keep
inviting her until New Year's Eve.

18:13.100 --> 18:15.070
She'll definitely agree eventually.

18:15.370 --> 18:21.160
However, President Kurata stopped
answering her phone after that.

18:23.760 --> 18:26.250
And so, New Year's Eve arrives.

18:28.920 --> 18:33.370
That's a weirdly nice sleep,
I even woke up on my own...

18:35.430 --> 18:36.380
Huh?

18:36.530 --> 18:40.000
It ran out of batteries?!
You got to be kidding me!

18:40.060 --> 18:43.480
I lectured Mob to always be punctual,
and now look at me!

18:45.230 --> 18:47.560
What, Tome isn't coming?

18:47.930 --> 18:49.080
Yeah...

18:49.080 --> 18:51.570
We ended up losing contact with her.

18:51.570 --> 18:54.990
But I'm sure she'll be happy
if we show her some UFO photos.

18:55.080 --> 18:56.410
You're right.

18:56.610 --> 18:59.580
We've made it this far,
let's make sure we find those UFOs.

19:04.360 --> 19:05.760
She's actually here.

19:05.760 --> 19:07.890
Faster than anybody else, to boot.

19:08.010 --> 19:10.320
What's this all about,
President Kurata?

19:10.390 --> 19:11.990
What about your training camp?

19:12.080 --> 19:14.280
Yeah, I'm skipping that.

19:14.720 --> 19:17.240
What, am I not supposed to be here?

19:17.350 --> 19:18.550
No, but...

19:18.550 --> 19:20.920
Why didn't you answer your phone?

19:21.000 --> 19:24.320
Oh, that? I broke my phone,
so I didn't realize.

19:24.460 --> 19:26.150
The heck?

19:26.520 --> 19:30.140
So, who's the telepath you guys found?

19:30.280 --> 19:32.090
She still doesn't know?

19:32.090 --> 19:34.560
Yeah, I thought she wouldn't
come if we told her.

19:34.890 --> 19:37.480
The meeting time is 9 AM, right?

19:37.480 --> 19:39.440
Let's wait for a little bit.

19:41.940 --> 19:44.820
Right, they're totally not coming.

19:45.840 --> 19:48.640
Why won't he pick up his phone?!

19:50.490 --> 19:54.040
Is it okay to make
your master wait this long?

19:54.600 --> 19:55.930
I'm not sure.

19:55.930 --> 19:57.950
I sent a message telling
the situation earlier,

19:57.950 --> 19:59.510
but he didn't reply.

19:59.630 --> 20:02.130
We might have to call this off...

20:03.560 --> 20:05.860
You're so freaking late, Takenaka!

20:06.920 --> 20:08.930
My bad, I overslept.

20:09.110 --> 20:10.760
Takenaka?

20:10.970 --> 20:13.110
What the heck are you doing here?

20:13.200 --> 20:15.970
Sorry I'm late.

20:16.080 --> 20:17.840
President Kurata.

20:18.000 --> 20:20.300
I'm the telepath.

20:21.060 --> 20:22.250
What?

20:22.250 --> 20:25.720
What is this?
Are you guys messing with me?

20:26.080 --> 20:30.640
Well, now that everyone's here,
let's head to the parking lot.

20:30.780 --> 20:31.920
Run for it!!

20:31.920 --> 20:35.330
Hurry up! He might be angry
and already left!

20:36.280 --> 20:37.950
He's here!

20:38.880 --> 20:41.730
I'm sorry we took a while, Master.

20:41.820 --> 20:44.320
Oh, don't worry about it.

20:44.430 --> 20:48.170
It's New Year's Eve,
let's take it easy.

20:48.410 --> 20:50.770
He just arrived two minutes ago.

20:53.550 --> 20:56.550
O-okay, let's go.

20:56.750 --> 20:59.240
Please drive safely.

20:59.380 --> 21:03.450
Please don't talk for a while.

21:07.510 --> 21:10.890
How could you oversleep on
an important day like this?

21:11.480 --> 21:13.690
I had a hard time sleeping.

21:13.690 --> 21:16.350
Was others' thought too loud again?

21:16.460 --> 21:18.440
No, I was nervous.

21:18.440 --> 21:20.720
It's been a while since
I've done anything like this.

21:20.720 --> 21:22.480
I see.

21:22.860 --> 21:26.510
-President, do you want some gum?
-Hmph, no.

21:26.890 --> 21:29.100
Can't believe you guys
actually tricked me.

21:29.100 --> 21:31.430
Takenaka's a telepath? Hah.

21:31.560 --> 21:34.190
-No, he's the real deal.
-It's okay.

21:34.190 --> 21:38.060
I don't even know if I can call
a UFO or not either.

21:40.570 --> 21:43.210
Approaching destination.

21:43.300 --> 21:45.340
Oh, so this is the place?

21:45.500 --> 21:47.360
It's Mud Boat Mountain.

21:47.470 --> 21:49.950
It's going to be full of winding
mountain roads from here.

21:49.950 --> 21:53.460
Don't get carsick before
we find the UFO, okay?

21:55.370 --> 22:00.210
The blue light shined
Dazzling my eye at 01:30 AM

22:00.250 --> 22:05.590
Even as I swiped the page over,
The smiles of friends besides me remain

22:15.600 --> 22:18.020
Yes, I want someone to understand

22:18.020 --> 22:20.520
All the colorless and transparent wishes

22:20.520 --> 22:23.020
All the breath stuck within
The depth of my heart

22:23.020 --> 22:25.650
Suddenly flowed out
Bringing my consciousness back

22:25.650 --> 22:28.110
I remember the days hung dry

22:28.110 --> 22:30.620
The very normal days passed by

22:30.620 --> 22:33.080
Even if reality is corrupted

22:33.080 --> 22:35.830
The sky we saw together
Was definitely real

22:36.410 --> 22:40.540
It's harder to understand than
The grammar on the blackboard

22:40.540 --> 22:45.760
The story that disappears
Under 24 hours makes me sad and lonely

22:46.010 --> 22:50.220
It's so hard, and I find myself
On the verge of giving up again and again

22:50.220 --> 22:51.760
But I...

22:52.600 --> 22:55.930
The current me will no longer give up

22:56.060 --> 23:00.940
Overflowing emotions on my sleeve,
Running through worry and doubt

23:00.940 --> 23:03.573
Nobody has decided
if the future is 0 or 100,

23:03.575 --> 23:06.150
So I'll paint over them myself

23:06.150 --> 23:08.541
Even if my existence itself
can't be proven,

23:08.543 --> 23:11.571
If this world struck me in my heart

23:11.700 --> 23:14.240
I will flood it with cobalt blue

23:26.200 --> 23:27.960
Hysteria from carsickness
and forgetting to bring things.

23:27.960 --> 23:30.060
Many things happened,
but we reached the summit.

23:30.060 --> 23:32.500
Now, time to show the power
of the Brainwave Club!

23:32.640 --> 23:34.610
Next on episode eight of
Mob Psycho 100 III,

23:34.610 --> 23:36.760
"Communicating 2
~Close Encounters of the Third Kind~"

23:36.870 --> 23:39.870
Watching from overseas?
Of course, that is a wise decision.
